You are my special.

12
00:01:05,420 --> 00:01:08,860
Now I'm not sure how to go.

13
00:01:38,860 --> 00:01:42,240
I don't want you to be able to do it.

14
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:45,057
I don't want you to be able to.

15
00:01:45,140 --> 00:01:50,997
I should make you cry,
you're a little devil.

16
00:01:51,080 --> 00:01:54,597
I make it so much you are my special.

17
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:58,997
I don't want you to be able to do it.

18
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:07,917
I should make you cry,
you're a little devil. You

19
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:15,000
are

20
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:21,330
aware

21
00:02:21,413 --> 00:02:22,243
of my technique,

22
00:02:22,326 --> 00:02:23,156
aren't you?

23
00:02:23,260 --> 00:02:25,900
I have the ability to control crows.

24
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:27,160
That's it.

25
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:28,760
Sounds weak, huh?

26
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:32,717
That's why I trained so
diligently ever since I was young.

27
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:35,741
I wanted to be able to
fight without my technique.

28
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:38,500
It wasn't a waste of my time.

29
00:02:38,820 --> 00:02:41,820
Being able to overwhelm
you like this proves it.

30
00:02:42,460 --> 00:02:43,290
Stop!

31
00:02:43,380 --> 00:02:45,037
I'll pull out of this right now!

32
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:46,120
I swear I will!

33
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:47,299
Somebody spare me!

34
00:02:47,880 --> 00:02:51,527
You're interrupting my sister,
and she's not finished talking.

35
00:02:52,260 --> 00:02:57,080
I used to tell myself that a sorcerer's
true value wasn't their technique.

36
00:02:57,760 --> 00:03:00,557
But eventually, I hit my limit.

37
00:03:00,640 --> 00:03:03,237
I couldn't keep improving
my physical abilities

38
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:06,144
and enhancing myself with
cursed energy forever.

39
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:07,620
I was crushed.

40
00:03:08,300 --> 00:03:09,820
I had lost heart.

41
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:13,240
So I decided to embrace and
master my own technique.

42
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:18,560
And that's when I came into full
bloom as a grade one sorcerer.

43
00:03:25,940 --> 00:03:26,770
Applause.

44
00:03:32,860 --> 00:03:34,240
No, I'll kill you.

45
00:03:35,380 --> 00:03:38,357
I just wanted to kill some
time chatting for a while.

46
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:39,560
Promise, I'm sorry!

47
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:41,160
I won't be bad again!

48
00:03:41,980 --> 00:03:42,810
Please!

49
00:03:42,893 --> 00:03:43,740
Please spare my life!

50
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:46,320
Hey, Wee Wee.

51
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:47,580
Tell me something.

52
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:52,057
How do you suppose one measures the
weight and value of a single life?

53
00:03:52,140 --> 00:03:52,970
That's easy!

54
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:56,669
It all depends how valuable
that life is to you, big sister!

55
00:03:58,260 --> 00:04:04,800
Thank you and you i uh well i guess

56
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:10,037
You can't immediately
describe the scale you use to

57
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:13,537
measure the lives you hunt
down That's the reason why you

58
00:04:13,620 --> 00:04:18,777
lost and just so you know what
i think about it I measure

59
00:04:18,860 --> 00:04:21,919
lives by their service
potential that's what matters

60
00:04:37,480 --> 00:04:38,310
Huh?

61
00:04:38,393 --> 00:04:41,497
How come only the veil that was
keeping sorcerers out got lifted?

62
00:04:41,580 --> 00:04:45,797
They all should have lifted since we
just broke three of these with Eno.

63
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:50,880
Either they used all three to lower
one veil, or two of them were dummies.

64
00:04:52,460 --> 00:04:55,578
Regardless, sorcerers can
move freely in Shibuya now.

65
00:04:55,880 --> 00:04:58,597
That just leaves the veil
that's trapping Gojo,

66
00:04:58,680 --> 00:05:01,327
and the veil that's
trapping ordinary people.

67
00:05:01,700 --> 00:05:05,297
I wanted to ask this geezer more
questions, but he won't wake up.

68
00:05:05,380 --> 00:05:06,615
We should rejoin Eno.

69
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:09,310
Eno!

70
00:05:36,300 --> 00:05:38,160
The veil's lifted.

71
00:05:39,580 --> 00:05:41,140
What now, Granny?

72
00:05:42,140 --> 00:05:46,980
What if we do now?

73
00:05:47,520 --> 00:05:52,737
It won't hurt to keep Satoru Gojo out of
play for a while longer, so go down there!

74
00:05:52,820 --> 00:05:55,114
and kill as many sorcerers as you find.

75
00:05:59,460 --> 00:06:00,290
Ransun?

76
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:09,096
Who the hell do you think
you're ordering around, Hag?

77
00:06:13,380 --> 00:06:15,000
What's the meaning of this?

78
00:06:15,160 --> 00:06:18,660
I only channeled the body's
information, not the soul's.

79
00:06:20,180 --> 00:06:21,010
...channeled.

80
00:06:21,160 --> 00:06:23,180
Ah, now I get it.

81
00:06:23,900 --> 00:06:25,240
This can't be.

82
00:06:25,580 --> 00:06:28,077
I've always made it a point
not to channel the soul

83
00:06:28,160 --> 00:06:31,336
in order to prevent accidents
like this ahead of time.

84
00:06:32,140 --> 00:06:36,460
I'm not sure exactly why, but
my body has always been special.

85
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:40,388
I guess that's why your grandson's
soul lost against my body.

86
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:43,200
A soul losing to a body?

87
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:45,510
No!

88
00:06:45,593 --> 00:06:46,500
That's impossible!

89
00:06:48,020 --> 00:06:49,360
Kill sorcerers, huh?

90
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:55,400
You're a sorcerer.

91
00:07:00,100 --> 00:07:01,580
They really hit Ijichi?

92
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:10,317
It sounded like he got attacked
while on the phone with Nita.

93
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:13,377
So it probably happened after
he left Fushiguro's group.

94
00:07:13,460 --> 00:07:14,813
He might be in trouble.

95
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:18,100
Nobara, go with Akari to Ijichi.

96
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:20,837
We can't use our cell phones in here,

97
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:24,377
so we won't get anywhere without
the assistant supervisors.

98
00:07:24,460 --> 00:07:26,931
I doubt that idiot Satoru would ever lose,

99
00:07:27,140 --> 00:07:30,081
but this whole situation
is smelling even fishier.

100
00:07:30,640 --> 00:07:32,875
I'll take care of things here for now.

101
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:36,459
That old man is completely useless.

102
00:07:39,540 --> 00:07:40,370
Ignore him.

103
00:07:40,780 --> 00:07:41,610
Now go!

104
00:07:42,100 --> 00:07:42,930
Right!

105
00:07:45,880 --> 00:07:49,760
Worst case scenario, once they're
outside the Veil, they can run.

106
00:07:52,700 --> 00:07:53,640
How is he?

107
00:07:54,760 --> 00:07:56,597
He's not doing well.

108
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:57,860
But he's not dead.

109
00:07:58,660 --> 00:08:01,120
I'm gonna knock them out! He's a dory.

110
00:08:01,380 --> 00:08:03,297
I understand how you feel, alright?

111
00:08:03,380 --> 00:08:05,851
But what's our highest priority right now?

112
00:08:06,980 --> 00:08:07,980
Rescuing Gojo.

113
00:08:08,340 --> 00:08:09,693
The Veil's been lifted.

114
00:08:09,840 --> 00:08:12,257
The people at the top might
have escaped already anyway.

115
00:08:12,340 --> 00:08:15,634
Anyway, I'll take Eno with
me and head outside the veil.

116
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:21,800
Okay, you take care of Eno.

117
00:08:21,980 --> 00:08:23,657
I'll go on ahead to the station.

118
00:08:23,740 --> 00:08:25,622
I agree, that's the best course.

119
00:08:25,840 --> 00:08:28,781
But operating alone in
Shibuya right now is not...

120
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:32,240
Alright, good. But if you... I know.

121
00:08:32,420 --> 00:08:33,857
If I die, you'll kill me.

122
00:08:33,940 --> 00:08:34,770
Am I right?

123
00:08:38,580 --> 00:08:39,777
Don't worry so much.

124
00:08:39,860 --> 00:08:41,400
I have Mechamaru with me.

125
00:08:41,920 --> 00:08:45,332
Though, I haven't heard anything
from him for a while now.

126
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:47,724
Just as long as you understand.

127
00:08:49,500 --> 00:08:50,480
See you later.

128
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:52,750
Yeah!

129
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:56,840
Fix this.

130
00:08:56,980 --> 00:08:58,627
Looks like the veil is gone.

131
00:08:59,120 --> 00:08:59,950
Oh boy.

132
00:09:00,240 --> 00:09:04,416
The thought of how much I'll get for
making Satoru Gojo owe me a favor.

133
00:09:05,500 --> 00:09:07,240
It just makes my heart raise.

134
00:09:08,180 --> 00:09:10,160
That was faster than expected.

135
00:09:17,340 --> 00:09:18,400
Nita, stop!

136
00:09:20,440 --> 00:09:23,680
Oh, it's a woman in a suit!

137
00:09:24,860 --> 00:09:27,720
Oh, I'm so happy.

138
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:30,700
I was getting sick of them all being men.

139
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:33,320
Nita, you better go hide.

140
00:09:33,560 --> 00:09:35,340
I'm gonna finish this quickly.

141
00:09:45,580 --> 00:09:50,168
In fact, pretend to hide in Bunkamura,
then keep going and slip through Tokyo.

142
00:09:51,220 --> 00:09:54,517
From the way he's talking, he
probably took out Eiji-chi,

143
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:56,306
which means we need to hurry.

144
00:09:56,500 --> 00:09:57,330
Right.

145
00:09:58,180 --> 00:10:00,474
Kugisaki, don't push yourself too hard.

146
00:10:00,860 --> 00:10:02,331
Whispering to each other?

147
00:10:02,580 --> 00:10:04,140
Now you've got me curious!

148
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:09,150
Aww!

149
00:10:09,960 --> 00:10:11,480
Aww, she's going to hide.

150
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:18,550
Whoa!

151
00:10:19,480 --> 00:10:23,127
You must be throwing the match
if you're coming at me unarmed.

152
00:10:24,300 --> 00:10:25,771
Didn't I meet you before?

153
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:33,637
Most who rely on cursed tools
are mid - or long-range fighters,

154
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:35,014
so keep up the attack.

155
00:10:36,340 --> 00:10:37,987
Remind me who you are again!

156
00:10:52,120 --> 00:10:54,355
Shooting nails is dangerous, you know.

157
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:57,327
Oh, I'll make it even
more dangerous for you.

158
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:05,130
Hey.

159
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:08,640
So she wasn't hiding after all.

160
00:11:15,460 --> 00:11:16,290
Nika!

161
00:11:18,820 --> 00:11:19,920
He shoots!

162
00:11:20,940 --> 00:11:21,770
Scores!

163
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:27,480
Why, you...

164
00:11:32,140 --> 00:11:33,717
The sword he dropped earlier...

165
00:11:33,800 --> 00:11:35,857
Where did it come from?

166
00:11:35,940 --> 00:11:36,940
Uh…

167
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:38,630
Huh…

168
00:11:38,713 --> 00:11:39,800
Hiya!

169
00:11:42,940 --> 00:11:43,770
Too bad!

170
00:11:44,940 --> 00:11:45,770
Hairpin!

171
00:12:01,940 --> 00:12:02,770
Nita!

172
00:12:22,640 --> 00:12:25,880
Yeah, you really are
dangerous, aren't you?

173
00:12:28,800 --> 00:12:31,000
Aw, did it hit your chin?

174
00:12:32,100 --> 00:12:34,560
Hey, can't you stand?

175
00:12:36,280 --> 00:12:37,440
Hello? You there?

176
00:12:38,620 --> 00:12:42,860
Gotta say, you've gotten an awful
lot stronger since we last met.

177
00:12:43,200 --> 00:12:45,800
I didn't even recognize you at first.

178
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:51,700
But being strong isn't enough
to win in this world, you know.

179
00:12:52,260 --> 00:12:54,700
Especially when my technique is involved.

180
00:12:56,160 --> 00:12:57,797
Although, believe it or not,

181
00:12:57,880 --> 00:13:01,233
I don't really understand my
own technique all that well.

182
00:13:05,580 --> 00:13:09,600
Now then, which of you
should I kill first?

183
00:13:10,820 --> 00:13:11,650
What?

184
00:13:13,680 --> 00:13:14,510
Huh?

185
00:13:15,560 --> 00:13:16,560
Work, mouth work!

186
00:13:17,460 --> 00:13:19,380
What are you after?

187
00:13:20,560 --> 00:13:22,266
Buy as much time as possible!

188
00:13:22,620 --> 00:13:26,620
Uh, they said something about
wanting to seal Satoru Gojo.

189
00:13:27,100 --> 00:13:30,180
I was asking you what you want.

190
00:13:31,380 --> 00:13:32,640
Oh, really?

191
00:13:35,520 --> 00:13:38,637
What do you think someone with
a great talent and love for

192
00:13:38,720 --> 00:13:42,260
soccer would do if they were
born in a world without soccer?

193
00:13:42,900 --> 00:13:44,560
No, that's not right.

194
00:13:44,980 --> 00:13:46,680
I can't explain it well.

195
00:13:47,820 --> 00:13:50,620
Although, is the reason
really that important?

196
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:52,880
I mean, who cares?

197
00:13:53,060 --> 00:13:55,280
The whole thing's fun, right?

198
00:13:55,700 --> 00:13:59,140
As long as I keep having fun,
what else really matters?

199
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:02,620
Wouldn't you agree, Leia?

200
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:04,780
Cut it out!

201
00:14:13,560 --> 00:14:15,260
Oh, ow!

202
00:14:17,120 --> 00:14:19,420
Please, don't let me commit any.

203
00:14:23,720 --> 00:14:25,740
Oh, I'm full of fun.

204
00:14:35,820 --> 00:14:37,100
Watch where you step!

205
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:47,520
Yeah, yeah!

206
00:15:12,480 --> 00:15:14,360
Ooh, look at this.

207
00:15:15,040 --> 00:15:17,864
I get to kill people that
aren't in black suits.

208
00:15:32,140 --> 00:15:34,760
He must have come to
Shibuya with Fushiguro.

209
00:15:36,700 --> 00:15:37,530
Nanami.

210
00:15:45,840 --> 00:15:47,100
Come on now, man.

211
00:15:47,260 --> 00:15:48,357
Just look around you.

212
00:15:48,440 --> 00:15:50,357
You really sure you want to approach me?

213
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:53,911
I mean, can't you see I'm
holding a woman hush-skitch here?

214
00:15:56,280 --> 00:15:57,110
Huh?

215
00:15:58,320 --> 00:15:59,150
Huh?

216
00:15:59,233 --> 00:16:00,220
She ran away.

217
00:16:03,380 --> 00:16:05,300
How many are there?

218
00:16:05,620 --> 00:16:07,380
Allies and their locations.

219
00:16:10,020 --> 00:16:11,580
I don't know.

220
00:16:17,140 --> 00:16:19,217
A wall?

221
00:16:19,300 --> 00:16:21,377
I didn't cut him?

222
00:16:21,460 --> 00:16:22,880
Not a scratch.

223
00:16:23,460 --> 00:16:26,160
Number and locations of your allies.

224
00:16:26,860 --> 00:16:27,690
Now!

225
00:16:47,800 --> 00:16:49,600
Huh? Did I die?

226
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:53,005
No, but I would have died
without my technique.

227
00:16:53,920 --> 00:16:54,750
I...

228
00:16:54,833 --> 00:16:55,663
I have to run!

229
00:17:06,520 --> 00:17:11,340
The number of your allies
and their locations.

230
00:17:12,120 --> 00:17:14,220
I told you, I don't know!

231
00:17:37,860 --> 00:17:39,460
Nope, not this time.

232
00:17:39,800 --> 00:17:41,360
Hey, you weren't invited.

233
00:17:48,780 --> 00:17:53,760
On my way here, I found several
of our assistant supervisors dead.

234
00:17:55,760 --> 00:17:57,220
That was you, right?

235
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:03,940
I'm sorry.

236
00:18:26,100 --> 00:18:27,397
He's on another level.

237
00:18:27,480 --> 00:18:30,860
This is what it means to
be a grade one sorcerer.

238
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:34,460
Come on, let's make our way to Nita.

239
00:18:37,260 --> 00:18:39,320
Well, well, well, it's you.

240
00:18:42,280 --> 00:18:44,200
Mei Mei, it's been too long.

241
00:18:45,240 --> 00:18:49,060
Quite the thing to say after
sending an assassin after me, Code.

242
00:18:50,540 --> 00:18:52,000
How is he alive?

243
00:18:52,620 --> 00:18:54,540
Did Gojo screw up last year?

244
00:18:56,240 --> 00:18:59,887
Unless Gojo and Code were in on
this whole commotion together.

245
00:19:00,620 --> 00:19:02,460
No, definitely not.

246
00:19:02,840 --> 00:19:07,177
Gojo could kill every person in this
country all on his own if he wanted to.

247
00:19:07,260 --> 00:19:09,197
There'd be no need or point in setting up

248
00:19:09,280 --> 00:19:11,927
these tricks or getting
anyone else involved.

249
00:19:12,780 --> 00:19:16,280
I actually held you in higher
regard than Gojo, you know.

250
00:19:16,860 --> 00:19:20,213
That nihilistic smile of yours
was always quite charming.

251
00:19:20,640 --> 00:19:23,228
It's a shame that I'll
have to kill you now.

252
00:19:23,920 --> 00:19:25,820
And squash such potential.

253
00:19:26,400 --> 00:19:27,760
It's quite a shame.

254
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:29,830
Genuinely.

255
00:19:30,200 --> 00:19:32,120
This Code has got to be a fake.

256
00:19:32,640 --> 00:19:33,470
Mei Mei.

257
00:19:33,553 --> 00:19:35,020
I think it's a shame too.

258
00:19:36,160 --> 00:19:39,380
To think I'd have to go after
my former upperclassmen.

259
00:19:43,360 --> 00:19:44,480
First manipulation.

260
00:19:45,380 --> 00:19:46,700
Did I read this wrong?

261
00:19:47,760 --> 00:19:51,160
This is a special grade
disease curse. Smallpox deity.

262
00:19:51,600 --> 00:19:54,957
I used up my stock of cursed
spirits by the end of last year.

263
00:19:55,040 --> 00:19:56,780
But this is of good quality.

264
00:19:58,060 --> 00:20:02,020
Just to be safe, I want to keep
the humans on the B5 level.

265
00:20:02,680 --> 00:20:04,151
